WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.065 --> 00:00:03.827
The ghost spoke again, and his voice was quiet and low.

2
00:00:03.852 --> 00:00:08.192
"Have you ever read the old prophecy on the library window?" he asked.

3
00:00:08.193 --> 00:00:13.374
"Oh, often," said Virginia, turning from the tapestries on the walls to look at him.

4
00:00:13.375 --> 00:00:15.780
And she recited the verse from heart:

5
00:00:15.781 --> 00:00:17.281
When a golden girl can win

6
00:00:17.305 --> 00:00:19.891
Prayer from out the lips of sin,

7
00:00:19.891 --> 00:00:21.844
When the barren almond bears,

8
00:00:21.868 --> 00:00:24.650
And a little child gives away its tears,

9
00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:27.072
Then shall all the house be still

10
00:00:27.096 --> 00:00:29.686
And peace come to Canterville.

11
00:00:29.686 --> 00:00:32.949
"But I don't know what it means," she added.

12
00:00:32.949 --> 00:00:45.219
"It means," he said sadly, "that you must weep with me for my sins and pray with me for my soul, and if you have always been sweet and gentle and good, the Angel of Death will have mercy on me."

13
00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:49.354
A cold shudder ran through her, and she thought gravely for a moment.

14
00:00:49.355 --> 00:00:51.065
At last she stood up.

15
00:00:51.066 --> 00:00:56.446
"I am not afraid," she said firmly, "and I will ask the angel to have mercy on you."

16
00:00:56.447 --> 00:01:02.943
The ghost rose from his seat, and taking her hand, he bent over it with old-fashioned grace and kissed it.

17
00:01:02.944 --> 00:01:09.261
His fingers were as cold as ice, and his lips burned like fire, but Virginia did not tremble.

18
00:01:09.262 --> 00:01:14.689
Then, clutching her hand more tightly, Sir Simon of Canterville muttered an incantation.

19
00:01:14.690 --> 00:01:19.567
A cold, dark passage opened in the wall, and he pulled her quickly into it.

20
00:01:19.568 --> 00:01:27.675
As they passed out of the tapestry chamber, Virginia looked desperately over her shoulder and saw the figures in the tapestries behind her.

21
00:01:27.675 --> 00:01:33.808
The animals and huntsmen called out, "Beware, Virginia! Your family may never find you again."

22
00:01:33.808 --> 00:01:37.749
At dinnertime, Virginia's chair at the dining table stood empty.

23
00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:41.231
"Where is your sister?" Mr. Otis asked Washington.

24
00:01:41.232 --> 00:01:47.046
"She's probably in the garden getting flowers for the table," Washington answered. "I'll go get her."

25
00:01:47.047 --> 00:01:52.377
But he couldn't find her. When he came back, the family decided to look through the castle.

26
00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:56.000
Everyone spread out, calling Virginia's name in all the rooms.

27
00:01:56.001 --> 00:02:01.685
When the castle was thoroughly searched and there was no trace of her anywhere, they met in the library.

28
00:02:01.685 --> 00:02:03.541
They were all a little worried.

29
00:02:03.542 --> 00:02:07.724
It was now evening, and the light outside the tall windows was fading.

30
00:02:07.725 --> 00:02:13.061
"Perhaps she didn't come home after her ride with the duke," suggested Mr. Otis.

31
00:02:13.061 --> 00:02:17.585
"Maybe the Gypsies have taken her!" cried Mrs. Otis anxiously.

32
00:02:17.585 --> 00:02:20.899
"Let's not get frantic," Mr. Otis said calmly.

33
00:02:20.899 --> 00:02:24.971
"I'll ride over to the Cheshire estate right now. I'm sure she's there."

34
00:02:24.971 --> 00:02:30.110
While he was gone, Washington took a lamp outside and searched the castle grounds.

35
00:02:30.111 --> 00:02:34.658
His mother and the twins searched inside again, opening every closet and cupboard.

36
00:02:34.668 --> 00:02:40.941
A short while later, Mr. Otis returned with the Duke of Cheshire, and both their faces were creased with worry.

37
00:02:40.942 --> 00:02:46.790
When he had heard that Virginia was missing, the young duke had insisted on riding back to help with the search.

38
00:02:46.791 --> 00:02:52.003
On the way, they had stopped by the Gypsy camp, only to discover that the Gypsies had gone.

39
00:02:52.004 --> 00:02:59.542
It was evident that the Gypsies had left in a hurry, as their fire was still smoking and some plates had been left on the grass.

40
00:02:59.542 --> 00:03:12.146
Straight away, Mr. Otis sent Washington off to the train station to inquire if anyone fitting Virginia's description had been seen on the platform and to dispatch telegrams to the police in all the surrounding districts.

41
00:03:12.146 --> 00:03:20.523
Then he and the duke headed out into the night again to ride for Bexley, a village about four miles away that was known as a gathering place for Gypsies.

42
00:03:20.524 --> 00:03:24.315
They found not the slightest hint or sign of the missing girl.

43
00:03:24.315 --> 00:03:33.513
The Gypsies, too, were distressed to hear of Virginia's disappearance, as she had always said hello when she passed their camp, and they remembered her smiling face.

44
00:03:33.513 --> 00:03:42.078
Tired and dejected, Mr. Otis and the duke returned home to find the rest of the family, including Mrs. Umney, waiting at the castle gate with lanterns.

45
00:03:42.079 --> 00:03:44.480
There was nothing more that could be done.

46
00:03:44.481 --> 00:03:51.048
So everyone went inside to eat a sad and quiet meal, hoping that they would hear something from the police.

47
00:03:51.048 --> 00:04:00.752
Just as they were passing out of the dining room, the tall clock in the hall began to strike midnight, and when the last stroke sounded, they heard a crash and a sudden shrill cry.

48
00:04:00.753 --> 00:04:11.300
Dreadful thunder shook the castle, a piece of wooden paneling flew off the wall at the top of the staircase, and out onto the landing stepped Virginia, looking very pale and white.

49
00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:15.256
In her hands was a small jewelry box of tarnished silver.

50
00:04:15.257 --> 00:04:17.499
In a moment, they had all rushed up to her.

51
00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:22.827
Everyone hugged her, even the twins, and the young duke kissed her several times on the cheek.

52
00:04:22.827 --> 00:04:28.184
"Thank God you are safe," murmured Mrs. Otis as she put her arm around the trembling girl.

53
00:04:28.185 --> 00:04:31.557
"Where have you been?" said Mr. Otis rather angrily.

54
00:04:31.558 --> 00:04:34.802
"We've been riding all over the country looking for you!"

55
00:04:34.802 --> 00:04:38.970
"Father," said Virginia quietly, "I have been with the ghost.

56
00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:42.231
He is finally at peace, and you must come see him.

57
00:04:42.231 --> 00:04:48.065
He was really sorry for all that he had done, and he gave me this box of beautiful jewels before he left."

58
00:04:48.066 --> 00:04:50.605
The whole family gazed at her in amazement.

59
00:04:50.606 --> 00:04:57.260
With a serious look, she turned around and led them through the opening in the wall, and down a narrow secret corridor.

60
00:04:57.260 --> 00:05:05.394
Washington followed with a lighted candle, and when they came to the end, the flickering light showed a low room with one tiny barred window.

61
00:05:05.395 --> 00:05:08.225
Stretched out on the floor was a gaunt skeleton.

62
00:05:08.226 --> 00:05:17.114
Its ankle was chained to the stone wall, and its long, fleshless fingers seemed to grasp at a dusty, mold-filled jug placed just out of its reach.

63
00:05:17.115 --> 00:05:20.185
Virginia knelt down and touched the skeleton tenderly.

64
00:05:20.185 --> 00:05:24.940
"This is where Sir Simon died a horrible death by starvation," she explained.

65
00:05:24.940 --> 00:05:31.162
One of the twins went to the small window to look outside and figure out which wing of the castle they were in.

66
00:05:31.162 --> 00:05:33.059
"Look at that," he called.

67
00:05:33.059 --> 00:05:34.988
"The old almond tree has blossomed.

68
00:05:34.988 --> 00:05:37.456
I can see the flowers in the moonlight."

69
00:05:37.456 --> 00:05:44.753
"The angel has forgiven him," said Virginia, and as she slowly rose to her feet, the rest of her family looked at her in wonder.

70
00:05:44.754 --> 00:05:49.542
Four days after these curious incidents, there was a funeral at Canterville Castle.

71
00:05:49.543 --> 00:05:54.999
Eight black horses pulled an old-fashioned carriage that carried an ornately carved coffin.

72
00:05:54.999 --> 00:06:00.281
Draped over the coffin was a rich purple cloth embroidered with the Canterville coat of arms.

73
00:06:00.281 --> 00:06:07.923
Lord and Lady Canterville came up to the castle to lead the procession for their ancient ancestor, and Virginia rode with them in their carriage.

74
00:06:07.923 --> 00:06:15.319
The coffin was lowered into a deep grave under the spreading branches of the almond tree in a quiet corner of the graveyard behind the castle.

75
00:06:15.319 --> 00:06:23.077
Years later the Duke of Cheshire and his beautiful duchess were visiting Canterville Castle to see Virginia's parents.

76
00:06:23.077 --> 00:06:31.140
The young couple had been married the year after Sir Simon's funeral, and at the ceremony everyone had admired the rare jewels she wore.

77
00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:39.171
Whenever she visited the castle, Virginia walked the quiet path to the almond tree to lay a flower on Sir Simon's gravestone.

78
00:06:39.171 --> 00:06:45.853
That evening, as she and her husband sat together in the moonlight, a nightingale began to sing in the branches above.

79
00:06:45.854 --> 00:06:52.124
Virginia quietly remembered the ghost's description of the Garden of Death, when her husband took hold of her hand.

80
00:06:52.125 --> 00:06:57.541
"Virginia," he said, "you never told me what happened when you were locked up with the ghost."

81
00:06:57.542 --> 00:07:02.206
"Please don't ask me, dear. It is something I cannot tell," she said.

82
00:07:02.206 --> 00:07:04.047
She looked at him and paused.

83
00:07:04.048 --> 00:07:12.265
"Except to say, he made me see what life is, and what death means, and why love is stronger than both."

